{
  "name": "e7_controls_jetson",
  "description": "E7 - the controls the design asks for and the runs that were missing. CPU INT8 separates the accelerator's hardware gain from its data-width gain, and probes the A78AE/A53 asymmetry (the A78AE has asimddp, the A53 does not). Timing at the extremes of the sweep shows the FP16-over-INT8 result is not specific to one ratio. Energy runs archive their raw power series, which is what a power-trace figure needs. CPU FP32 predictions are saved for the qualitative strip.",
